{
  "_about": "The ONE ordered chain map for dispatch.py. Every hook is a LINK here (its own file, run as a subprocess); settings.json registers dispatch.py once per event. Link types: gate|mutator|advisory|exec. exec links with \"async\": true are spawned detached and never waited on. tools = regex FULL-matched against tool_name. enabled toggles a link off without deleting it. priority 0 = mandatory advisory (never budget-dropped); higher = droppable once gates blew the wall budget. budgets.ms is that advisory-drop threshold only, not a rung of the timeout ladder: every link timeout_ms is above it by design, and the real ladder is harness timeout > sum of the sequential link timeouts (tests/test_timeout_ladder.py). timeout_ms is per-link. \"defer\": true (advisories) = spawned detached, text delivered on the session's next PreToolUse/PostToolUse; --only runs it synchronously. Pass order: gates+mutators in declared order, execs, advisories. CLAUDE_HOOK_DOCTOR stops detached writers (index builds, dox sweeps), not telemetry or gate state: point CLAUDE_HOOK_TELEMETRY_DIR and CLAUDE_HOOK_STATE_DIR at temp dirs to isolate a run (tests do, via conftest.py); hooks/.state is not redirected yet. Every budgets.chars stays under Claude Code's 8,000-char additionalContext cap: above it the harness saves the text to a file and shows the model a 2 KB preview.",
  "budgets": {
    "session-start": {"ms": 2500, "chars": 7800},
    "pre-tool-use": {"ms": 2000, "chars": 7800},
    "post-tool-use": {"ms": 1500, "chars": 7800},
    "post-tool-use-failure": {"ms": 800, "chars": 1500},
    "stop": {"ms": 2500, "chars": 4000},
    "subagent-start": {"ms": 800, "chars": 3000},
    "subagent-stop": {"ms": 1000, "chars": 2000},
    "pre-compact": {"ms": 800, "chars": 2000},
    "post-compact": {"ms": 1500, "chars": 6000},
    "config-change": {"ms": 1500, "chars": 500},
    "teammate-idle": {"ms": 1500, "chars": 1000},
    "session-end": {"ms": 1000, "chars": 0}
  },
  "chains": {
    "session-start": [
